RESEARCH
	Interesting/relevant mechanics from the list https://boardgamedesignlab.com/mechanism-master-list/
		Action drafting - shared pool of available actions
		Action points - resource for selecting certain actions
		Action / event - choose between action points or event execution; others could gain the opposite effect
		Action queue - local or global creation of sequence of actions
		Action retrieval - actions as a resource, once spent, it needs to be retrieved to be spent again
		Advantage token - passable token that permits a special action
		Area majority / influence - proportional benefit in a shared occupied space
		Area movement - game board is divided into areas that determine adjacency and movement 
		Area-impulse - turn subdivision to have smaller movement actions until exhaustion (TI4 action phase)
		Auction: sealed bid - players secretly make a bid, then reveal simultaneously
		Betting & bluffing: players commit a stake of currency or resources to purchase a chance of winning everyone’s stake
		Bribery: offer bribes to other players to get them to perform specific actions
	"Maybe" mechanics:
		Auction / bidding - take control of items by spending resources in a competing manner with other players
		Auction: dutch - selection of items for bidding starts expensive and the cost goes down gradually
		Auction: fixed placement - bids are places on lots, players can outbid each other, highest bidder for each lot wins
		Bias: pieces automatically move in a certain direction, or it is easier to move in a certain direction

